# Pervaxis Platform — C# Coding Standards

## File Layout

Every `.cs` file must start with the Clarivex license header (see `CLAUDE.md`).

Use **file-scoped namespaces**:

```csharp
namespace {{ model.names.namespace }}.Services;   // file-scoped — not block-scoped
```

## Class Design

- **Seal concrete classes** unless designed for inheritance: `public sealed class MyService`
- **Prefer `sealed record` for immutable value objects** and domain models
- **Prefer primary constructors** (C# 12) for simple DI — only if all dependencies are readonly
- No partial classes except `Program` (required for `WebApplicationFactory`)

## Async

- `ConfigureAwait(false)` on **every** `await` in library/service code — never in ASP.NET Core middleware
- Never block async code with `.Result`, `.Wait()`, or `GetAwaiter().GetResult()`
- Pass `CancellationToken` through every async call chain; use `ct` as the parameter name
- Use `IAsyncEnumerable<T>` for server-streaming results instead of `List<T>`

## Null Safety

- Nullable reference types are enabled (`<Nullable>enable</Nullable>`) — no `#nullable` overrides
- Use `ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(param)` at public API entry points
- Use `ArgumentException.ThrowIfNullOrWhiteSpace(param)` for string inputs
- Prefer `is not null` over `!= null`; prefer pattern matching over casting

## Time

- Use `DateTimeOffset.UtcNow` — never `DateTime.Now` or `DateTime.UtcNow`
- Store and transfer timestamps as `long` (Unix milliseconds) in proto; convert at the gRPC boundary
- Use `TimeProvider` (injected) in testable code instead of static `DateTimeOffset.UtcNow`

## Logging

```csharp
// Correct — structured properties, not string interpolation
_logger.LogInformation("Processing record {RecordId} for {Actor}", id, actor);

// Wrong — string interpolation loses structured log fields
_logger.LogInformation($"Processing record {id} for {actor}");
```

## Error Handling

- Catch the most specific exception type first
- **Always** catch `OperationCanceledException` separately — never treat cancellation as an error
- Map domain exceptions to `RpcException` with the correct `StatusCode` at the gRPC boundary
- Never swallow exceptions silently — at minimum, log before re-throwing

```csharp
catch (OperationCanceledException)
{
    // Cancellation is not an error — don't log as error, don't increment error metrics
    throw;
}
catch (YourDomainNotFoundException ex)
{
    _logger.LogWarning("Record not found: {RecordId}", ex.RecordId);
    throw new RpcException(new Status(StatusCode.NotFound, ex.Message));
}
```

## Dependency Injection

- Register services as `AddScoped` (per-request) unless they are truly stateless (`AddSingleton`)
- **Never** inject `IServiceProvider` directly into a service — use constructor injection
- Use `IOptions<T>` for configuration; validate with `[Required]`, `[Range]` on the options class
- Register `AddOptions<T>().ValidateDataAnnotations().ValidateOnStart()` for all options

## Code Quality

- `TreatWarningsAsErrors=true` is enforced — fix all Roslyn warnings before committing
- `AnalysisMode=All` is active — do not suppress analyzer warnings without a documented reason
- No TODOs in committed code without a linked Pervaxis Jira ticket: `// TODO [PERVAXIS-1234]`
- No commented-out code blocks — delete dead code, use git history to recover
- 90% line coverage is a CI gate — tests must be written alongside every new service method

## Formatting

- `dotnet format` enforces style — run before committing (`dotnet format --verify-no-changes` in CI)
- 4-space indentation, no tabs
- Opening braces on the same line (Allman style is not used)
- `var` for local variables when the type is obvious from the right-hand side
